 services, package damage, or executor-created temporary residue. The invalid `ss -H` cleanup check was diagnostic and caused no mutation; a subsequent compatible check directly confirmed cleanup.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c1e89bd66bc54ef9","cmd-beac7ad5a69f445d","cmd-c7212fbea1f7436e","cmd-343cf89c776e4787","cmd-3280bdcf325c4691","cmd-37be1e02d3a14d80","cmd-f01af6a1a3074d06","cmd-2bf640dec7304fa8","cmd-cfccd491ef0147bf","cmd-07e2e2130f604209","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct configuration, behavioral, reboot-persistence, and recovery evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was completed coherently on node1, node2, and node3: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered SSH, filesystem/network state, and relevant firewall behavior.","limitations":["The catch-all behavior was directly tested from node3 rather than from every possible external address; coverage of all other sources is established by the inspected ordered IPv4/IPv6 catch-all REJECT rules and their packet counters.","The fixed lifecycle listening-socket observations are empty even though executor probes directly observed SSH and temporary test listeners; therefore socket-specific conclusions rely on the more explicit executor evidence."]}
